{"c":[{"id":"99b0cde49d41360f","sum":"Live Jev: run live sets once (R1's slow-eval never settles; each pass sends 43-81 new requests). Keep HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false: on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T015102Z-70f8faec6a3a0648","text":"R1's slow-eval runner never settles on live Jev: each pass sends 43-81 new requests, so a set costs about 3x one pass. Run live sets once.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T015102Z-cf129cc10068e635","text":"HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS changes Jev's answers: with it on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms. Keep it false (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5678229122db2693","sum":"W1-W2: run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts each batch; --verifier refuse writes 0 outside exemptions, and new exempt (c) writes need a look. Value rules go in the write contract (fill/contract.ts), not beside a caller; labelled multi-value lines offer parts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T020955Z-5dafeedfea56fda2","text":"W1: canned evals never pick a plausible wrong candidate; run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts (offline, ~2 s) each batch: class (a) writes must stay 0. A labelled multi-value line offers its parts, not its whole (line-values severalValues).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T025421Z-86d442b2d62eead8","text":"Any path that writes a chosen value into a field checks fill/writable.ts writeMisfit (fill, planner validate, codeplan, offer filter, goal gate); add new value rules there, not beside one caller. Candidates are only added, never swapped out.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
